#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Availability Heuristic 🧠]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Tendency to overestimate likelihood based on memory availability 📊]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Example: Overestimating plane crash risk after seeing news reports 🛩️💥]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Leads to biased probability judgments 📉]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("The availability heuristic is a cognitive bias where people tend to overestimate the likelihood of events based on how easily examples come to mind.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For instance, after seeing news reports about a plane crash, people might overestimate the risk of plane crashes, because the examples are readily available in their memory.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("This heuristic leads to biased probability judgments, as the availability of examples in memory doesn't necessarily correspond to their actual frequency or probability.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Impact on Financial Decisions 💰]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Overestimating likelihood of memorable financial events 📈📉]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Example: Overestimating risk of stock market crash after 2008 financial crisis 📉]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Can lead to suboptimal investment decisions 🙅‍♂️💸]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In the context of financial decision-making, the availability heuristic can cause people to overestimate the likelihood of memorable financial events.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For example, after the 2008 financial crisis, many investors might have overestimated the risk of another imminent stock market crash, because the memory of the crisis was so vivid.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("This can lead to suboptimal investment decisions, such as avoiding the stock market altogether, even when it might offer good long-term returns.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Mitigating the Availability Heuristic 🛡️]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Be aware of the bias 🧐]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Seek out objective probability data 📊]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Consider alternative scenarios 🔍]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("To mitigate the effects of the availability heuristic, the first step is to be aware of the bias and how it can influence your judgments.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("When making financial decisions, seek out objective probability data rather than relying on memorable examples.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Also, make an effort to consider alternative scenarios, not just the ones that are readily available in your memory.")
]
]

